        "original_id": "56525882-c8a6-5ba3-968a-174bc1f04fbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: H. forsteriana, newly germinated seedlings, palm seeds\n- Places: Northern Hemisphere, Lord Howe Island, Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, Indian Ocean islands, Pacific Ocean islands\n- Organizations: Linospadicinae\n- Concepts: indoor plants, palm seed industry, trade, plant distribution, palm taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- H. forsteriana is commonly grown as an indoor plant in the Northern Hemisphere.\n- The two Howea species form the mainstay of Lord Howe Island's palm seed industry.\n- The two Howea species are even more important to Lord Howe Island's trade in newly germinated seedlings.\n- Bulbophyllum is found throughout most of the warmer parts of the world, including Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, and islands in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.\n- Linospadicinae is a subtribe of palm trees.\n- Linospadicinae includes the genera Howea and Linospadix.",
